# Firmware build outputs
firmware/**/build/
firmware/**/sdkconfig
firmware/**/sdkconfig.old
firmware/**/managed_components/

# NOT dependencies.lock — it is tracked on purpose.
#
# Ignoring it meant every clone re-solved the component graph against the live
# registry instead of the versions we build with, so the repo was unbuildable
# by anyone but the machine that had a stale local solve. That is the root
# cause of BufferRoot/Modulus-Firmware#2: esp_lvgl_port drifted to 2.9.0
# (needs on_frame_buf_complete, absent in IDF 6.0.1), esp-audio-player 1.0.7
# broke on GCC 15, and esp_wifi_remote resolved differently.
# managed_components/ stays ignored — it is the cache the lock reproduces.

# Vendor reference clone
vendor/

